Package: cade
Type: Package
Title: Composition Attribution of Differential Expression
Version: 6.0.0
Authors@R: person("Cheng", "Hu", email = "2024184006@hrbmu.edu.cn",
                  role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
                  comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0009-4627-0229"))
Description: Decomposes the observed log2 fold change of each gene in a bulk
    transcriptome comparison into a component implied by a change in cell-type
    composition and a residual component, and gates that decomposition with
    explicit diagnostics. The residual is an algebraic remainder: it equals the
    case group's deviation from the reference minus the control group's
    deviation, and is not a within-cell effect unless the control group can be
    shown to match the reference. Provides
    calibration that separates filtering by expression level (valid) from
    filtering by effect size (circular), reference-quality checks including a
    dual-reference comparison, automatic input validation that stops on a
    log-scaled or misaligned reference, a known-answer self test, and a
    pseudo-bulk simulator. Version 3 adds uncertainty-propagating decomposition with
      calibrated intervals, empirical null calibration of the residual from
      normal-versus-normal comparisons, and reference diagnostics. Version 4
      adds consistency diagnostics: marker-based calibration of the composition
      term per cell type, and cross-cohort agreement of the composition term
      versus the observed change, which shows that the former is reproducible
      across cohorts while the latter is platform-limited. Version 5 closes a
      silent misalignment bug: genes present in obs but absent from mu were
      previously recycled by position, giving wrong residuals with no error. Version 6 adds five functions and
    two breaking changes: `convention` selects mean-of-log
    (limma-compatible, now the default) or log-of-mean, which differ by 0.14
    in the comp-obs correlation on real data; `null_permutation()` supplies an
    exact permutation test over reference columns; `cor_ci()` requires the
    resampling unit to be stated; `calibrate_by_layer()` fits calibration per
    anatomical layer; `verify_deposit()` performs deposit-integrity checks
    A1-A3; and `granularity_crossed()` runs the reference-granularity crossed
    design, whose r is computed without deconvolution and whose absolute
    values are therefore not comparable with the companion paper. The framework
      is described in Hu (2026)
    <doi:10.5281/zenodo.23598561>.
